    <div class="pz-hero-quickanswer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> African greys are known for exceptional talking ability and problem-solving intelligence that's above average even among parrots, which means they need more daily mental challenge than most pet birds to avoid boredom-driven feather plucking. They need a large cage, several hours of supervised out-of-cage time, a diet built around pellets and fresh vegetables, and consistent daily interaction, since this species can bond tightly and struggle with sudden changes in routine.</div>
