function pz_what_is_african_grey_parrot_care() {
    ob_start(); ?>
    <p>This guide covers what's specific to caring for an African grey parrot (Psittacus erithacus), a medium-to-large parrot widely known for its talking ability and problem-solving skills. It focuses on what sets this species apart from other pet parrots rather than general bird-care basics.</p>
    <p>African greys are frequently cited among the most capable talkers and mimics in the parrot world, and owners and keepers consistently describe them working through small problems — opening latches, solving puzzle toys — in ways that stand out even among other parrot species. That intelligence is a double-edged trait for an owner: a bored African grey doesn't just sit quietly, it tends to find its own outlet, which is often feather plucking or repetitive behavior.</p>
    <p>This species also has a reputation for forming an unusually strong attachment to one person or routine, and for reacting to disruption, a new household member, a moved cage, a changed schedule, more noticeably than some other parrot species.</p>
    <?php return ob_get_clean();
}

